Description: wayland: Follow a surface's desktop depth with kde_stereo_content_v1 version 3
 .
 kde_stereo_content_manager_v1.get_depth creates a kde_stereo_depth_v1 for a
 surface, so a toolkit that draws a surface's elements once per eye can learn
 whether the surface may show depth inside it now, and which of its edges lie
 on its output's edge (the depth_state event), mark its pair as the desktop's
 own depth rather than stereo content (set_desktop_depth), and declare where a
 popup surface sits (set_place, unset_place).
 .
 A surface may have any number of these objects, since a toolkit and its style
 follow the same surface, independently of its stereo content declaration.
 The mark is the surface's while any of its objects sets it, the place is the
 one set last, both double-buffered and withdrawn with the object that set
 them; the objects become inert once the surface is gone. SurfaceInterface
 keeps the state the compositor last gave the surface and tells a new object
 at once; only changes are sent.
 .
 The protocol text is the plasma-wayland-protocols fork's version 3. KWin now
 takes the in-tree copy while the installed PlasmaWaylandProtocols lacks
 kde_stereo_depth_v1.
