-<interface name="kde_stereo_content_manager_v1" version="2">
+<interface name="kde_stereo_content_manager_v1" version="3">
   <description summary="declare stereo content of surfaces">
     A program tells the compositor that a surface's picture holds two
     views, one per eye, packed full side by side, with the left eye first.
     The compositor renders the declared surface once per eye with that
     eye's view. The global being present announces support.
 
+    Since version 3, a program may also follow a surface's desktop depth
+    with get_depth, to draw the elements inside the surface at their own
+    depths.
+
     Clients may use this protocol to declare stereo content. The version 1
     wire values are stable; future requests must use a new interface version.
     Destroying the manager does not affect declarations it created.
